      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of hardcoding the compiler filter here, I think it will be better to change global.SystemServerCompilerFilter to \"speed-profile\", and have the following logic here:\n\nif global.SystemServerCompilerFilter \u003d\u003d \"speed-profile\" {\n  if (the module has profile) {\n    compilerFilter \u003d \"speed-profile\"\n  } else {\n    compilerFilter \u003d \"speed\"\n  }\n} else if global.SystemServerCompilerFilter !\u003d \"\" {\n  compilerFilter \u003d global.SystemServerCompilerFilter\n}\n\nThere are a few benefits of doing this:\n1. It keeps the compiler filter configurable.\n2. Currently, only \"services\" has profile, so we get the desired behavior without explicitly special-casing \"services\".\n3. If we want to use speed-profile for APEX jars, we can just add profile to them, and we don\u0027t have to change the logic here.\n4. It makes Soong align with the behavior of odrefresh (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:art/odrefresh/odrefresh.cc;l\u003d1610-1614;drc\u003d099f0e7d092e6a390a046d67f3dac32189e92dd3). No changes need to be made to odrefresh.",
